<title>USA: Toshiba to begin making PC's - N.Y. Times.</title>
<headline>Toshiba to begin making PC's - N.Y. Times.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Toshiba Corp will announce on Tuesday its plans to enter the personal computers market with a strategy of making the machines more like ordinary home appliances, the New York Times reported.</p>
<p>The three models under the brand name Infinia will be capable of receiving television and radio signals, play compact discs and serve as a telephone answering machine.</p>
<p>The article said the computers will come with Intel Corp microprocessors, and are expected to range in price from about $2,150 to $3,250.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
</text>
